              {
                "uuid": "1966e5a3-144c-4f10-9bde-345a75ac714c",
                "control-id": "ia-5",
                "description": "Tunnel tokens are sender-constrained: a bearer token is refused, and each request carries a fresh DPoP proof signed by the key the token is bound to. The relay never stores a token. Its own registration key is generated in the FIPS module, written with mode 0600 (or 0640 when owned by root), refused when readable by others, read only from its directory, and never sent: registration carries only the public key.",
